# UI Rules

Use XML layouts only. Use View Binding. Follow Material Design (Material 3 components).

## Layout

Prefer

- ConstraintLayout for screens
- RecyclerView + ListAdapter for lists
- Material Components (`MaterialTextView`, `MaterialButton`, `MaterialToolbar`, ...)

Avoid

- Deep nested layouts
- Unnecessary ViewGroups
- `findViewById`, Kotlin synthetics, data binding expressions

## Naming

- Layouts: `activity_*.xml`, `fragment_*.xml`, `item_*.xml`, `dialog_*.xml`
- Drawables: `bg_*`, `ic_*`, `flag_*`
- View ids: snake_case (`btn_app_theme`, `mtv_version`) so ViewBinding produces readable camelCase.

## Dimensions and Text

- Spacing / sizes: `@dimen/_16sdp` (sdp).
- Text: `@dimen/_14ssp` (ssp) or `sp`. Never `dp` for text.
- No hardcoded `px`.

## Theme (light / dark)

Every screen must work in light and dark theme.

- Base theme parent must stay a `DayNight` theme.
- Semantic colors live in `values/colors.xml`; dark overrides in `values-night/colors.xml`.
- Use semantic tokens in layouts and drawables: `surfaceColor`, `onSurfaceTitle`, `onSurfaceMessage`, `onSurfaceHint`, `surfaceVariant`, `cardBackground`, `onCardTitle`, `onCardMessage`, `outlineColor`, `rippleColor`, `navSelected`, `navUnselected`, `navIndicator`, `tab*`.
- Never reference raw palette colors (`neutral500`, `primary100`, `white`, `black`) from a layout or drawable, unless the color is intentionally identical in both themes (for example white text on a primary-colored button).
- Never hardcode a hex color in a layout, drawable, or vector. Add a token instead.
- New vector icons must reference `@color/...` for fills that need to flip with the theme.
- A new semantic color MUST be added to both `values/colors.xml` and `values-night/colors.xml`.

Theme behaviour

- Follows the system by default (`AppTheme.SYSTEM`).
- Manual switching through `applyAppTheme(mode)` in `helpers/theme/ThemeHelper.kt`.
- Selection persisted in `SharedPrefManager.appThemeMode` and restored in `MainApplication.onCreate`.

## Localization

- Every user-visible string goes in `values/strings.xml`. Never hardcode text in a layout or in Kotlin.
- Mark non-translatable values with `translatable="false"`.
- The project ships `values-<lang>/strings.xml` for many locales; add the new key to the default file at minimum and state that translations are pending.
- Language switching goes through `helpers/locale/LocaleHelper.applyLanguage(code)` (AppCompat per-app locales) and `SharedPrefManager.appLanguageCode`.

## Accessibility

Always

- Set `contentDescription`, or `importantForAccessibility="no"` for decorative images.
- Support dynamic font scaling (no fixed-height text containers).
- Respect minimum touch target size (48dp).
- Keep sufficient contrast in BOTH themes.

## Edge to Edge

Activities extend `BaseActivity`, which enables edge-to-edge and applies system bar insets.

Choose the inset behaviour by overriding `getInsetsMode()` with an `InsetsMode` value
(`EDGE_TO_EDGE`, `TOP`, `BOTTOM`, `TOP_BOTTOM`).

Do not re-implement inset handling inside a screen.

## UI Logic

Keep UI logic and state in the ViewModel. Fragments only render state and forward events.
